      <!-- SECTION 4: SEO prose -->
      <section class="neutral-bg">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="prose">
            <h2>Dragon vs Windows built-in voice tools</h2>
            <p>Windows 11 includes Voice Typing (Win+H) and Voice Access - both require an internet connection per Microsoft's own documentation. Dragon Professional 16, once installed and activated, operates without an internet connection. For professionals working with sensitive documents, in environments with limited connectivity, or requiring consistent accuracy with specialised vocabulary, this distinction is significant.</p>
            <h2>Dragon Professional 16 vs Speech Recognition Cloud</h2>
            <p>Dragon and Speech Recognition Cloud serve different needs. Dragon is a locally installed, offline-capable, English-only product built for deep workflow integration - custom vocabulary, voice macros, audio file transcription, and hands-free PC control. Speech Recognition Cloud is a cloud-based subscription that works instantly with no voice training, supports 57+ languages, and runs in any Windows application. The right choice depends on your connectivity requirements, language needs, and whether you want a locally installed or cloud-based solution.</p>
            <h2>What Dragon Professional 16 does not do</h2>
            <p>Dragon Professional 16 is designed for single-speaker dictation and transcription. It will not reliably transcribe multi-speaker conversations, meetings, or interviews. It is a Windows-only product - Nuance discontinued Dragon for Mac. It supports English only across six regional variants (Australian, New Zealand, UK, US, Canadian, and Indian English). For cloud-hosted or virtual desktop deployments, consider Dragon Professional Anywhere.</p>
            <h2>System requirements</h2>
            <p>Dragon Professional 16 requires Windows 10 or Windows 11. Allow at least 12GB free disk space for installation. An internet connection is required for the initial download and activation, but not for ongoing use. Apple AirPods are not supported for live dictation - a dedicated USB headset or dictation microphone is recommended for best accuracy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
